ui-prefer-a-fab-without-a-label-when-the-icon-alone-is-universally-understood = Prefer a FAB without a label when the icon alone is universally understood

ui-an-extended-fab-is-a-single-container-with-a-leading-icon-and-a-label-keep-the-icon-option = An extended FAB is a single container with a leading icon and a label. Keep the icon optional: when the label already names the action, the icon only supports recognition.

ui-use-the-default-primary-container-tone-for-most-screens-secondary-and-tertiary-tones-separ = Use the default primary container tone for most screens. Secondary and tertiary tones separate a floating action from other primary-colored elements, and solid accent tones raise its emphasis.

ui-keep-one-tone-across-a-screen-so-the-floating-action-stays-identifiable = Keep one tone across a screen so the floating action stays identifiable.

ui-place-an-extended-fab-at-the-bottom-end-of-the-screen-above-the-bottom-navigation-bar-or-a = Place an extended FAB at the bottom end of the screen, above the bottom navigation bar or any bottom sheet. Keep a 16dp margin from the screen edges and from other floating elements.

